  "body": "### What is the issue with the Infra Standard?\n\nSeveral specs seem to create a promise without defining what \"promise\" is, e.g. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-img-decode\n\n> Let promise be a new promise.\n\nMost of them eventually return and expose it via Web IDL `Promise`, which is [defined as a JS Promise](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-promise). But if we start to use it internally in the spec, like https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/pull/251 and https://github.com/w3c/screen-orientation/pull/269 intend to do (and like [Streams](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/) does all over its internal slots), things are less clear what those promises are intended to be.\n\nHaving an infra definition referring to JS Promise would be helpful for that.",
